    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d823">

                <pb facs="0854" n="752" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg752"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">8621.01/274a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan (Grew)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-09-05T17:00:00-04:00">September 5, 1933—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>76. Associated press telegram from Tokyo under date September 1st reports that
                    the Japanese Navy Office issued a statement to vernacular <pb facs="0855"
                        n="753" xml:id="pg753"/> newspapers in regard to Japanese harbor works in
                    the Mandated Pacific Islands part of which read “Those islands are Japanese
                    territory”. Telegraph whether this translation is accurate and send full
                    Japanese text by pouch.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
